WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.569
I jumped out of the barrel and dived behind the foresail when I heard feet pound across the deck.

2
00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:15.569
Then I joined Hunter and Dr. Livesey in the rush to see the land that had been sighted.

3
00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:23.450
The fog began to lift about the same time the moon appeared, and we saw two hills a couple of miles apart on the island.

4
00:00:23.451 --> 00:00:30.657
Rising behind them was a third, higher hill whose peak was still buried in fog.

5
00:00:30.658 --> 00:00:35.970
"Men," Captain Smollett said, "has anyone ever seen that island before?"

6
00:00:35.971 --> 00:00:42.231
"I have, sir," Long John said. "I was there once with a merchant ship."

7
00:00:42.232 --> 00:00:47.179
"Can we safely drop anchor on the south side?" the captain asked.

8
00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:55.688
"Aye, sir," replied Long John. "That small bit of land is called Skeleton Island—it was a place for pirates once.

9
00:00:55.689 --> 00:01:02.018
The three hills on the main island are Foremast Hill, Main Hill, and Mizzen Hill.

10
00:01:02.019 --> 00:01:09.039
The pirates kept a lookout on Main Hill when they were anchored, so they called it Spyglass Hill."

11
00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:13.845
"I have a chart here," Captain Smollett said. "See if that's the place."

12
00:01:13.846 --> 00:01:21.945
Long John's eyes gleamed eagerly as he took the chart, but it wasn't the map we found in Billy Bones' chest.

13
00:01:21.946 --> 00:01:30.618
It was a copy that was complete except for the red crosses and the written notes—the information that would lead anyone to the treasure.

14
00:01:30.619 --> 00:01:34.470
Long John hid his disappointment and annoyance.

15
00:01:34.471 --> 00:01:42.396
"Yes, sir," he said, "that's the spot. 'Captain Kidd's Anchorage'—that's what my shipmates called it.

16
00:01:42.397 --> 00:01:48.049
There's a strong current that runs along the south and then heads north along the west coast.

17
00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:51.131
You were very wise to slow down here.

18
00:01:51.132 --> 00:01:56.748
If you intend to stay for a time, there's no better place for the ship."

19
00:01:56.749 --> 00:02:01.794
"Thank you," Captain Smollett said. "I'll ask for your help later. You may go."

20
00:02:01.795 --> 00:02:07.320
I was surprised by how cool Long John was, admitting he knew the island.

21
00:02:07.321 --> 00:02:15.146
Then he came near me and laid his hand on my arm, and I could scarcely conceal a shudder.

22
00:02:15.147 --> 00:02:25.726
"Ah," he said, "this island is a sweet spot for a lad. You'll swim, climb trees, and run up the hills like a goat.

23
00:02:25.727 --> 00:02:30.038
Tell me when you want to go exploring, and I'll make up a snack for you."

24
00:02:30.039 --> 00:02:34.101
Then he clapped me on the shoulder and hobbled off.

25
00:02:34.102 --> 00:02:40.157
Captain Smollett, the squire, and Dr. Livesey were talking together on the quarterdeck.

26
00:02:40.158 --> 00:02:45.344
I was anxious, but I dared not interrupt them while the crew was listening.

27
00:02:45.345 --> 00:02:51.214
I was trying to think of some way to get their attention when Dr. Livesey called to me.

28
00:02:51.215 --> 00:02:54.655
"Jim, fetch my pipe for me!" he said.

29
00:02:54.656 --> 00:03:01.519
I ran and got his pipe, and when I gave it to him, I whispered, "Doctor, please do as I say.

30
00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:08.258
Get the captain and squire down to the cabin, and then send for me. I have terrible news."

31
00:03:08.259 --> 00:03:14.800
The doctor's face turned serious, but he recovered quickly. "Thank you, Jim," he said quite loudly.

32
00:03:14.801 --> 00:03:21.545
Then, acting as if he'd asked me a question, he added, "That was all I wanted to know."

33
00:03:21.546 --> 00:03:27.153
The doctor then rejoined Captain Smollett and the squire as they looked toward the island.

34
00:03:27.154 --> 00:03:34.765
They spoke together, and though no one made a move, it was clear Dr. Livesey had communicated my request.

35
00:03:34.766 --> 00:03:38.672
"Mr. Anderson, summon the men," the captain ordered.

36
00:03:38.673 --> 00:03:44.212
Job blew a few notes on his pipe and the crew assembled on deck.

37
00:03:44.213 --> 00:03:48.997
"My lads," Captain Smollett said, "you have all performed your duties admirably,

38
00:03:48.998 --> 00:03:53.844
so Mr. Trelawney wants you to have a drink to celebrate a job well done.

39
00:03:53.845 --> 00:03:59.163
He and I and the doctor are going below for a few moments, and then you will have some rum.

40
00:03:59.164 --> 00:04:04.434
If you agree, let's give Mr. Trelawney a good sea cheer."

41
00:04:04.435 --> 00:04:12.876
The cheer followed, and it rang out so full and hearty, I could hardly believe these same men were plotting to kill us.

42
00:04:12.877 --> 00:04:20.661
"A cheer for Captain Smollett too!" Long John added, and this cheer was also shouted with enthusiasm.

43
00:04:20.662 --> 00:04:29.334
The three gentlemen went below, and not long after, word was sent that Jim Hawkins was wanted in the captain's cabin.

44
00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:38.823
When I arrived, all three were seated around the table, and the doctor was smoking with his wig in his lap, a sign he was agitated.

45
00:04:38.824 --> 00:04:43.220
"Now, Hawkins," Trelawney said, "speak up."

46
00:04:43.221 --> 00:04:47.593
I told them what I'd heard, and nobody interrupted.

47
00:04:47.594 --> 00:04:54.264
"Captain," Trelawney said finally, "you were right, and I was wrong. I'll admit it."

48
00:04:54.265 --> 00:05:02.108
"I must have missed some clues too," the captain returned, "for I never heard of a crew planning to mutiny without any warning signs."

49
00:05:02.109 --> 00:05:06.950
"It's Silver's influence," said the doctor. "He's a remarkable man."

50
00:05:06.951 --> 00:05:11.153
"He'd look remarkably good hanging from the rigging," the captain said.

51
00:05:11.154 --> 00:05:16.579
"Well, we can't turn back. If I ordered them to turn around, they'd attack us at once.

52
00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:22.301
We have some time—at least until this treasure's found— but we'll have to fight them sooner or later.

53
00:05:22.302 --> 00:05:25.617
I propose we hit them when they least expect it.

54
00:05:25.618 --> 00:05:28.804
Can we count on your servants, Mr. Trelawney?"

55
00:05:28.805 --> 00:05:31.656
"Definitely," the squire declared.

56
00:05:31.657 --> 00:05:37.482
"That's three men," the captain said. "Add the rest of us and that makes seven, including Hawkins here.

57
00:05:37.483 --> 00:05:39.596
Can we count on any more men?"

58
00:05:39.597 --> 00:05:44.542
"The men Trelawney hired before he met Silver should be honest," replied the doctor.

59
00:05:44.543 --> 00:05:49.722
"We can't rely on them," the squire said. "Israel was one of those men."

60
00:05:49.723 --> 00:05:53.373
"Well, gentlemen," said the captain, "keep your eyes and ears open.

61
00:05:53.374 --> 00:05:56.934
We can do nothing until we know who's with us."

62
00:05:56.935 --> 00:06:02.459
"Jim can help," the doctor said. "The men like him, and Jim notices everything."

63
00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:06.860
"Hawkins, I'm putting my faith in you," said the squire.

64
00:06:06.861 --> 00:06:10.922
I felt desperate and helpless because we were so outnumbered.

65
00:06:10.923 --> 00:06:20.377
Right now, the grown men on our side were six to the pirates' nineteen.

